{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the word נבוב לחת.</b> Like the Aramaic translation, and similar to it ואיש נבוב ילבב (Job 11:12), which means empty without heart, in the manner of those who say 'a head without brains.' Now, the basin was not mentioned because it was not made from the donation of all Israel, but only from the donation of the women alone; therefore it is mentioned with the section of the spices, which all Israel did not bring — only the princes alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:41.639642227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}